{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>You shall not do according to all that we do here</b>, etc. Scripture suspended the prohibition of bamot upon the building of the Temple, because the Temple had not yet been built and they had not yet rested from their enemies, and they were pressed by war, and they would have feared to all come to offer their sacrifices in one place. And so it is written nearby: 'and He will give you rest from all your enemies,' etc., 'and it shall be the place that YHWH will choose,' etc. And so David said: 'And it came to pass, when the king sat in his house, and HaShem had given him rest from all his enemies round about, that the king said to Nathan: Behold, I dwell in a house of cedars, but the ark of Elohim dwells within curtains.' And now HaShem has given me rest round about — there is no adversary and no evil occurrence — and now I say to build a house,' etc." "<b>Every man whatsoever is right in his own eyes.</b> As Rashi explained. And one should not interpret <b>whatsoever is right in his own eyes</b> to mean that each man would make a bamah on his roof or in his courtyard, for the bamot were forbidden in the wilderness, as it is written: 'and to the entrance of the Tent of Meeting they did not bring it,' etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:33.976807615Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}